  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses specifically on the presence of a zero outcome and prefers the lottery without it. The individual explicitly acknowledges the 1% chance of getting nothing in B, which shows they considered the presence of a zero outcome. Their justification includes this fact as a reason to avoid B. While their overall reasoning is broader—incorporating certainty, risk aversion, and payoff differences—the presence of the zero outcome in B is clearly part of their deliberation. The decision reason’s rule (prefer the lottery without a zero outcome) aligns with the individual’s attention to and negative evaluation of the 1% chance of zero in B. Although the individual uses a more general risk-averse rationale, the core element of avoiding a zero outcome is present and contributes to the decision. Therefore, it is highly likely that the decision reason was used, even if embedded within a broader risk-aversion framework.",
  "final_assessment_score": 90
